        "end_s": 40.5,
        "headline": "Drawer-front depth increases during closure",
        "detail": "The marked right-side drawer-front regions show increasing camera-relative depth while the upper-cabinet reference stays nearly unchanged, supporting the visible inward motion. These are region medians, not tracked-point displacement or calibrated travel distance.",
        "observation": "At 27.0, 31.5, 36.0 and 40.5 s, drawer-front region medians are 559, 578, 606 and 637 stored units; the upper-cabinet reference medians are 546, 547, 546 and 547. Both regions have fully valid readings at these samples.",
        "claim": "The drawer-front surface recedes relative to the camera during the closing push, with a 78-unit difference between the first and last sampled region medians.",
        "alternative": "The drawer region is repositioned between samples and does not track one physical point, so surface orientation and changing sampled patches may contribute to the numerical difference.",
